# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Mustfile — Physical state contract for hermeneia
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# What MUST be true about this repository. Hard requirements.
# Run with: must check
# Fix with: must fix (where a deterministic fix exists)

@abstract:
Physical-state invariants for hermeneia. These are hard requirements — CI and
pre-commit hooks fail if any check fails.

This file was inherited from rsr-template-repo and, at instantiation (issue #8),
five of its invariants were found to be FALSE against this tree: they named the
template's own paths and markers rather than hermeneia's. A contractile that
declares invariants which do not hold is worse than one that declares fewer, so
each was either corrected to the real path or replaced by a check that is true
and load-bearing. What is asserted below was executed against this tree before
it was written down.
@end

## File Presence

### license-present
- description: LICENSE file must exist
- run: test -f LICENSE
- severity: critical

### readme-present
- description: README.adoc must exist
- run: test -f README.adoc
- severity: critical

### security-policy
- description: A SECURITY policy must exist (root or .github/, .md or .adoc)
- run: test -f SECURITY.md || test -f SECURITY.adoc || test -f .github/SECURITY.md
- severity: critical
- notes: |
    Was `test -f SECURITY.md` and FALSE here — this repo's policy lives at
    .github/SECURITY.md, which is the estate-canonical location
    (.machine_readable/root-allow.txt records the tension: openssf-compliance
    and scorecard accept either, this contractile accepted only the root).
    Widened to the same set openssf-compliance.yml accepts, so the contractile
    and the CI gate cannot disagree about what satisfies the obligation.

### ai-manifest
- description: 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml must exist
- run: test -f 0-AI-MANIFEST.a2ml
- severity: critical

### governance-docs
- description: GOVERNANCE.adoc, MAINTAINERS.adoc, CODEOWNERS must exist
- run: test -f GOVERNANCE.adoc && test -f MAINTAINERS.adoc && test -f .github/CODEOWNERS
- severity: critical

### machine-readable-dir
- description: .machine_readable/ directory must exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable
- severity: critical

## Directory Structure

### contractiles-complete
- description: All required contractile directories exist
- run: test -d .machine_readable/contractiles && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/bust && test -d .machine_readable/contractiles/dust
- severity: critical

### contractiles-files-present
- description: All four primary contractile files exist, each in its verb directory
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/intend/Intentfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/must/Mustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/trust/Trustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/adjust/Adjustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical
- notes: |
    Was the flat `.machine_readable/contractiles/<Verb>file.a2ml` layout and
    FALSE here — this repo uses the per-verb directory layout
    (intend/, must/, trust/, adjust/, bust/, dust/) that the sibling
    bust-dust-files-present invariant already assumes. The two invariants
    contradicted each other; this one was the stale half.

### bust-dust-files-present
- description: Bustfile and Dustfile exist in their directories
- run: test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/contractiles/dust/Dustfile.a2ml
- severity: critical

### six-directory-present
- description: descriptiles directory (the 6A2 descriptive family) exists with required files
- run: test -d .machine_readable/descriptiles && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/META.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/ECOSYSTEM.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/PLAYBOOK.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/AGENTIC.a2ml && test -f .machine_readable/descriptiles/NEUROSYM.a2ml
- severity: critical

### anchors-directory
- description: anchors directory exists in descriptiles/
- run: test -d .machine_readable/descriptiles/anchors
- severity: warning

### self-validating-structure
- description: self-validating directory has its examples and its methodology guard
- run: test -d .machine_readable/self-validating && test -d .machine_readable/self-validating/examples && test -f .machine_readable/self-validating/methodology-guard.k9.ncl
- severity: warning
- notes: |
    Was `test -d .../k9-svc` and FALSE — no k9-svc/ directory exists in this
    repo and nothing creates one. Asserting the files that ARE the structure
    (the k9 templates' examples/ and methodology-guard.k9.ncl, the validator
    that enforces this contractile's own state-validation rules) instead.

## Template Integrity

### no-placeholder-values
- description: No unfilled template placeholder token survives anywhere in the tree
- run: bash scripts/check-no-placeholders.sh .
- severity: critical
- notes: |
    Was `test -z "$(grep -r '{{' .machine_readable/contractiles/)"` and FALSE —
    that grep has no closing brace, so it matched just's own {{args}}
    interpolation in contractiles/Justfile and the word {{PLACEHOLDER}} used in
    Adjustfile.a2ml's prose about placeholders. It could only ever fail.
    Delegated to scripts/check-no-placeholders.sh, the single estate
    implementation of this rule (vendored from rsr-template-repo), which matches
    upper-snake tokens only, exempts metasyntactic ones, and allow-lists the
    template and example trees by path. One implementation, not a second copy
    that can drift from the CI gate.

### instantiation-rendered
- description: The tree is fully rendered from .machine_readable/configs/instantiation.a2ml
- run: bash scripts/instantiate.sh --check
- severity: critical
- notes: |
    REPLACES `template-readonly`, which grepped for an RSR_TEMPLATE_DO_NOT_EDIT
    marker that exists nowhere in this repository — an invariant that could only
    ever fail, guarding a condition (this is the template, do not edit it) that
    is not true of hermeneia.
    What this repo actually needs guarded is the regression that issue #8
    describes: the tree was scaffolded and never rendered, and nothing noticed
    for the repo's whole life. This asserts the rendered state is still true, so
    a template re-sync that reintroduces a token fails here rather than shipping.
    Companion CI check: openssf-compliance.yml runs the same gate.

## Git State

### no-untracked-contractiles
- description: All contractile files are tracked in git
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .machine_readable/contractiles/ 2>/dev/null)"
- severity: critical

### signed-commits
- description: All commits must be signed
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: critical
